    {
      "duration_ms": 12000,
      "caption": "Each cache line, typically 64 bytes, is in one of four states per core: M, E, S or I.",
      "narration": "With per-core caches, the same line can live in several places. MESI tracks each line's state: Modified, Exclusive, Shared or Invalid, so only one core can write at a time.",
      "elements": [
