        },
        {
          "id": "r",
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "Core 0 reads: miss, line goes E",
            "Core 1 reads: snoop hit",
            "Both copies become S"
          ],
          "x": 8,
          "y": 20.0,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 600,
          "enter": "slide-up",
          "color": "blue"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 12000,
      "caption": "A write to a Shared line broadcasts an invalidate; other copies become Invalid, the writer becomes Modified.",
      "narration": "To write, a core needs ownership. For a Shared line it sends an invalidate and waits for acknowledgments. A write miss issues a read-for-ownership. The writer ends in Modified.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Writes",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 6,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "w",
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "S + write: send invalidate",
            "I + write: RFO (read for ownership)",
            "Others: S/E -> I",
            "Writer: M"
          ],
          "x": 8,
          "y": 20.0,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 600,
          "enter": "slide-up",
          "color": "orange"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 12000,
      "caption": "A later read of a Modified line forces a write-back or a cache-to-cache transfer.",
      "narration": "If another core then reads a Modified line, the owner must supply the data or write it back. Both end in Shared. That transfer is why contended lines are slow.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Reading a Modified line",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 6,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "mm",
