    {
      "duration_ms": 11500,
      "caption": "Real chips add Owned or Forward states and use directories; false sharing bounces lines.",
      "narration": "Real protocols extend this. AMD uses MOESI with an Owned state, and large systems use directories rather than snooping. Two threads writing one line cause false sharing ping-pong.",
      "elements": [
